// A capture plan (`dev_capture::plan::CapturePlan`), the game's damage-model view (game state
// only): the player's own tank struck through its engine bay, shown in the glass look with the
// record's fields drawn as one volume (`pen_cam_look.wgsl` reading the depth pictures
// `pen_cam_picture.wgsl` renders). The offline target scenario `OVERMATCH_TARGET=fires` parks a
// target that fires into the player's engine at 25 s (`tank::scenario`, on `Time<Real>`, so this
// plan fixes no frame step). If that round knocks the tank out the frames show the kill cam's
// lesson, as in one run (MEASURED); if not, the x-ray, held on from 26 s by the offline-only
// scripted preference `OVERMATCH_XRAY`, dresses the live tank under the same record. In that one
// run the lesson drew the record's fields; `pen-cam-killcam.ron`'s round stopped in the
// ammunition and drew none (MEASURED, one run each). From the checkout root, hidden and silent
// under the machine's build lock:
//
//   /usr/bin/lockf -k -t 10800 /tmp/overmatch-cargo.lock env OVERMATCH_TARGET=fires \
//     OVERMATCH_XRAY=26-40 OVERMATCH_UNATTENDED=1 OVERMATCH_WINDOW=hidden \
//     OVERMATCH_CAPTURE=scripts/capture/pen-cam-glass.ron target/debug/overmatch --offline
//
// writes target/capture/pen-cam-glass-<second>.png at each frame second, then exits. Times and
// size are capture configuration (ASSUMED), not game data.
(
    frames: (
        out: "target/capture/pen-cam-glass.png",
        at: [27.0, 28.0],
        size: (1280, 720),
        scale_factor: 1.0,
        ui: false,
        gizmos: false,
    ),
)
